      "text": "The Manila City DRRM Office has raised the BLUE ALERT as a precaution against the possible effects of the Hanging Habagat, intensified by a Low-Pressure Area (LPA) east of the country.\n\nAccording to DOST-PAGASA and the city’s Resident Meteorologist, Manila may experience light to moderate, at times heavy, rains on Wednesday, August 27.\n\nResidents, especially those near coastal and low-lying areas, are advised to stay vigilant, monitor official updates, and follow authorities’ instructions to avoid possible flooding incidents. (📷: Manila DRRM Office) | via Diann Calucin",
